# The console's build context is this directory, so the repository root's
# .dockerignore never applied to it - Docker only reads the one next to the
# context. Without this file `COPY . .` copied the developer's own
# node_modules over the one pnpm had just installed in the image, and the
# build died on `Cannot find module '/src/node_modules/@angular/cli/bin/ng.js'`:
# pnpm's tree is full of symlinks into a store that does not exist in the
# container, and on Windows they are not even the same kind of link.
#
# It failed on every machine that had ever run `pnpm install` here and nowhere
# else, which is why CI - a clean checkout - never saw it (0100).
node_modules
dist
.angular

# Nothing the build needs, and every byte here is one copied into the daemon.
.vscode
*.log
